Package: zvolrescue
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Vladyslav V. Prodan <akapulko@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/click0/zvolrescue
Description: read-only extraction of zvols and files from ZFS pools that no longer import
 zvolrescue reads the on-disk format of a ZFS pool by itself, without
 the kernel's ZFS and without importing the pool, and writes the raw
 image of a volume out of it at any transaction group that still
 verifies: every block through its checksum, mirror copies and RAIDZ or
 dRAID parity to heal what one member cannot give, encrypted datasets
 with a key. It never writes to the members.
 .
 With it: zvoltimeline (the pool's history from the transaction groups
 it still carries), zvolcarve (volumes no uberblock points at any more,
 found in raw vdev space), zvolfiles (files out of filesystem datasets)
 and zvolreport (the evidence logs of the others as one signed,
 checkable report). The binaries are static and depend on nothing.
